/*
  NotionSidebar.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0175 · NotionSidebar (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Keys mirror the web source
  (components/layout/sidebar/NotionSidebar.tsx) `nav.*` namespace VERBATIM — the `t(key, default)` calls and
  the per-row `navLabel` labels — so every Swift literal routes through the facade fallback and the sources
  hold no hardcoded English. `{{page}}` / `{{count}}` slots are filled by NotionSidebarInterpolation (the
  native peer of i18next interpolation).

  Notion-specific copy vs. the Linear sibling: `nav.pages` ("Pages") backs the permanent group label, and
  `nav.pinPage` is "Pin {{page}}" (the web Notion default — NOT "Pin {{page}} to favorites").

  Two keys have no literal web string because the web owns the filter STATE but renders its typing surface
  upstream and leaves a bare "Pages" label for the no-data case; the native peer realizes both (a filter field
  + a friendly empty state), so each gets a localizable key here.

  The "notionSidebar.sample.*" entries back the DEBUG-only inspector + previews; they are never shipped.

  These entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in
  a per-surface table ("NotionSidebar") so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings.
*/

/* --- Shipped copy (verbatim from the web nav.* namespace) --- */
"nav.sidebar" = "Sidebar navigation";
"nav.favorites" = "Favorites";
"nav.pages" = "Pages";
"nav.filterNoMatch" = "No matches.";
"nav.filterClear" = "Clear filter";
"nav.pinPage" = "Pin {{page}}";
"nav.unpinPage" = "Unpin {{page}}";
"nav.vehicleCount" = "{{count}} vehicles";
"nav.staleCount" = "{{count}} stale rows";

/* --- Native-realized affordances (filter field + no-data empty state) --- */
"nav.filterPrompt" = "Filter";
"nav.empty" = "No navigation items.";

/* --- DEBUG inspector / preview sample copy (not shipped) --- */
